{"5447700":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"King of Billiards","steam_appid":5447700,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your cue. Your next move.<\/h2>King of Billiards brings you into a warmly lit billiards club with a low, first-person aiming view. Line up the shot with your mouse, hold Ctrl and move back and forward to strike, and hold Shift to raise the cue. Choose the cue-ball contact point for spin and find your own rhythm at the table.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A little precision. A little surprise.<\/h2>Play Chinese 8-ball, 9-ball and a casual Snooker ruleset, or try Skill Duel: each player receives three random cards per rack, while nine changing arena effects reshape the contest. Swap solids and stripes, split the cue ball, open portals, attract balls toward a pocket, or leave your opponent just one open pocket. Cards have their own timing and conditions; hold Alt to inspect your hand before making a move.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Learn the shot. Make it yours.<\/h2>Practise at your own pace, challenge the computer, or face another player over LAN or the internet. Steam players can host a room and invite friends. Raise the cue for controlled jumps, use cushion rebounds and carefully placed spin, and follow the action as the camera opens up after a shot. Optional aiming guides can be disabled for both players by the room host.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A club to return to<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Four rulesets, AI opponents, free practice and two-player matches.<br><\/li><li>25 skill cards and nine random arena effects in Skill Duel.<br><\/li><li>40 achievements for progress, match wins, shot-making and experimentation.<br><\/li><li>Table and cue styles, adjustable sensitivity and a choice of background music.<br><\/li><li>31 interface language options. Achievement descriptions currently support Chinese and English.<\/li><\/ul>This is a casual independent billiards game, not a professional referee simulator. The rulesets share the club table; Snooker does not use a separate full-size tournament table. Multiplayer uses a player host or the dedicated-server connection. Mouse and keyboard are required.","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your cue. Your next move.<\/h2>King of Billiards brings you into a warmly lit billiards club with a low, first-person aiming view. Line up the shot with your mouse, hold Ctrl and move back and forward to strike, and hold Shift to raise the cue. Choose the cue-ball contact point for spin and find your own rhythm at the table.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A little precision. A little surprise.<\/h2>Play Chinese 8-ball, 9-ball and a casual Snooker ruleset, or try Skill Duel: each player receives three random cards per rack, while nine changing arena effects reshape the contest. Swap solids and stripes, split the cue ball, open portals, attract balls toward a pocket, or leave your opponent just one open pocket. Cards have their own timing and conditions; hold Alt to inspect your hand before making a move.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Learn the shot. Make it yours.<\/h2>Practise at your own pace, challenge the computer, or face another player over LAN or the internet. Steam players can host a room and invite friends. Raise the cue for controlled jumps, use cushion rebounds and carefully placed spin, and follow the action as the camera opens up after a shot. Optional aiming guides can be disabled for both players by the room host.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A club to return to<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Four rulesets, AI opponents, free practice and two-player matches.<br><\/li><li>25 skill cards and nine random arena effects in Skill Duel.<br><\/li><li>40 achievements for progress, match wins, shot-making and experimentation.<br><\/li><li>Table and cue styles, adjustable sensitivity and a choice of background music.<br><\/li><li>31 interface language options. Achievement descriptions currently support Chinese and English.<\/li><\/ul>This is a casual independent billiards game, not a professional referee simulator. The rulesets share the club table; Snooker does not use a separate full-size tournament table. Multiplayer uses a player host or the dedicated-server connection. Mouse and keyboard are required.","short_description":"Take your place at the table. Aim with the mouse, feel every stroke, and play Chinese 8-ball, 9-ball, Snooker or Skill Duel. Jump over obstacles, change the table with skill cards, practise alone, or challenge AI and friends.","supported_languages":"English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Danish, Ukrainian, Russian, Bulgarian, Hungarian, Indonesian, Turkish, Greek, Norwegian, Czech, Japanese, Polish, Thai, Swedish, Romanian, Finnish, Dutch, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal, Spanish - Latin America, Vietnamese, Arabic, Korean, Malay","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5447700\/526c44c357f59013944a96a97c9e24a4a898a2db\/header.jpg?t=1793699626","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5447700\/7ff51bbd5380a267627e167f75d1d0f2f445d54f\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793699626","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5447700\/7ff51bbd5380a267627e167f75d1d0f2f445d54f\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793699626","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 11 (64-bit)<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> 64-bit quad-core processor<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8192 MB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Dedicated GPU with Vulkan 1.2 support<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1024 MB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Keyboard and mouse required. Internet connection required for online multiplayer.<\/li><\/ul>","r